1
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:12,220
With Inyaba in tow and
a new carriage to boot,

2
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,797
JoJo and crew arrived in
the coastal town of Karachi,

3
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:20,351
Pakistan's industrial and financial
center located in the Indus River Delta.

4
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:44,620
Thank you.

5
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:34,340
Take it out with vision to turn around.

6
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,680
Oh, hey, a Donner Kebab joint.

7
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,098
Let's stop and get something to eat.

8
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:13,960
The Donner Kebab.

9
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:16,757
It's been called the
hamburger of the Middle East.

10
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:21,140
A slab of meat is placed on a spit,
its outer layer roasting as it turns.

11
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,540
Before long, the meat is cooked,

12
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:27,271
sliced, and served with any
number of sides and condiments.

13
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:28,800
Excuse me, sir.

14
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,217
I'd like five of those.

15
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:31,829
That'll be a thousand yen.

16
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:33,210
Thousand yen?

17
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,080
In the Middle East,

18
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:39,097
Japanese and Western business
practices are by no means universal.

19
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:42,121
Namely, prices change and
are open to negotiation.

20
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:46,317
With no understanding of how to
haggle or how to value goods for sale,

21
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:49,697
first-time visitors can become
easy targets for exploitation.

22
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:53,360
But here, people don't see such
exploitation as a bad thing.

23
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:56,933
The swindled are deserving of
the label fool, not victim.

24
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:59,440
Haggling takes guts and ingenuity.

25
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:01,050
Really?

26
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:03,634
The first step is the art of the bluff.

27
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:05,777
Make it clear you see through the trick.

28
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:07,625
Let him know you're no slouch.

29
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:10,760
Don't mock me now.

30
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:13,337
That's far too much for
a handful of kebabs.

31
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:15,420
A hearty laugh always helps.

32
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,980
Then, how much would you buy him for?

33
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:20,300
The merchant will test the waters.

34
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:22,900
Make it 250 yen for five.

35
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:26,237
In return, you throw out a price so low?

36
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:28,840
You can't help but blush and then!

37
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:36,177
He'll act as if you have no
sense at all catching on?

38
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:39,057
If I sold them for that cheap,
I'd be out on the streets!

39
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:42,022
my wife and seven children
would starve to death!

40
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:48,497
Then he'll gesture the old throat slash,
but you can't give up the fight just yet!

41
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:51,317
Then maybe I'll just
buy them somewhere else?

42
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,957
pretend that you're leaving.

43
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:55,120
Okay, friend, you win.

44
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,897
I'm very much like foreigners.

45
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:59,080
I'll sell you five for 700 yen.

46
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,200
He'll try to stop you.

47
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:02,820
Then make it 300!

48
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:05,960
Let the haggling begin! 600!

49
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:08,040
350! 550!

50
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:10,040
400! 450!

51
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:14,040
425! I'll take him!

52
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:18,880
Alright, I got them for less than
half his original price. Take that!

53
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:20,897
I'm made out like a bandit.

54
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:23,340
and just as you think you won.

55
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:28,980
I usually sell five for 150
yen. Bye-bye. Thank you, sir.

56
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:40,400
Holy crap! Turn around!

57
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:41,954
That old lady's awake!

58
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:50,990
I...

59
00:04:51,073 --> 00:04:51,940
I promised you.

60
00:04:52,140 --> 00:04:54,964
I haven't said anything
to any of them, I swear.

61
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:56,840
Why are you here?

62
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:59,260
What could you possibly want with me?

63
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:03,117
Did you think I would actually tell
them the secret of Lord Dio's stand?

64
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,940
I am and shall always
be his loyal servant!

65
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:31,040
Gross! What are they?

66
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:32,318
Some kind of worms?

67
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:34,710
Why?

68
00:05:34,793 --> 00:05:36,000
I have done nothing wrong!

69
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:38,240
Why have you come here to kill me?

70
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:42,220
Lord Dio places his trust in no one.

71
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:44,180
Not even you and Yabba.

72
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,400
That is why.

73
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:49,180
And it's my job to make sure
that you never speak again.

74
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:52,960
As for the rest of you...

75
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:56,500
The only way you're leaving is in pieces.

76
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:01,350
Mime!

77
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,630
What?

78
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,220
You can call me Dan.

79
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:10,040
Dan of Steel.

80
00:06:10,740 --> 00:06:13,537
My stand represents the
one and only Lover's Card.

81
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:17,837
I will see to it that you all meet the
same fate as that pathetic witch Iniyaba.

82
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:18,820
How could you?

83
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:22,480
That old lady was one of your
own, you son of a... Memory!

84
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,550
Lies!

85
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:25,830
Lies!

86
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:29,120
These are all lies!

87
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,140
This isn't happening.

88
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:32,957
Lord Dio would never do this to me.

89
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:35,200
I am his loyal servant.

90
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:36,590
Loyal!

91
00:06:36,673 --> 00:06:40,617
These things coming out of her body,
they're definitely not some stand.

92
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:41,840
Don't you see it?

93
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:43,451
They're actual tentacles.

94
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:46,140
I have dedicated everything to him.

95
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:48,516
Lord Dio would never do me such harm.

96
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:52,120
He'd never plant a flesh bud in me.

97
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:53,440
What did she say?

98
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:56,860
Lord Dio is my only reason for living.

99
00:06:57,620 --> 00:06:59,700
We trust each other wholeheartedly.

100
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:01,620
Hold on!

101
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:09,850
See that?

102
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:12,260
The sun just disintegrated them.

103
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,440
The flesh bud.

104
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:15,600
It's made out of Dio's own cells.

105
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:17,090
Precisely.

106
00:07:17,173 --> 00:07:19,517
I must say you were
quite the perceptive one.

107
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,597
Since you're so astute, I'll continue.

108
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:23,977
This is what a full-grown
flesh bud looks like.

109
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:26,240
I want to kill her, not control her.

110
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:28,560
So I just grew it inside the old bag.

111
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:30,270
And yarba,

112
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:34,837
you may be the very one who told lord
dio about the stance but you're a

113
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:38,397
fool to think that a man with such
complete power would ever trust a feeble

114
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:44,357
old woman like you unfortunately
it's a point you fail to realize old

115
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:47,297
lady what's the true identity of dio

116
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:52,637
stan tell us you placed all your hope

117
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:56,477
in dio you trusted him with your
life and your sons and now after all

118
00:07:56,560 --> 00:08:00,217
you've sacrificed you know he's not
the man you thought he was you know i'm

119
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:06,337
right we must defeat dio no matter
the cost you have to tell us we need

120
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:10,940
to know tell us what we need to know
about dio's stand before it's too late

121
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:17,460
oh my lord

122
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:27,640
he believes in me

123
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:32,700
so i'll serve him even in
death i won't betray him

124
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,080
Oh, God!

125
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:47,720
How pathetic.

126
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:52,220
It's laughable how sad that old woman was.

127
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:55,937
But the very depth of her trust
in him should tell you something.

128
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:59,549
Lord Dio's evil charm is more
powerful than you can imagine.

129
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:12,960
The old woman may have had it out for us,

130
00:09:13,060 --> 00:09:16,001
but she was misled and
sure as hell didn't deserve

131
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:17,470
that death.

132
00:09:17,553 --> 00:09:18,797
I'll see you join her.

133
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:21,292
Four against one, but we won't hold back.

134
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:22,380
Prepare yourself,

135
00:09:28,780 --> 00:09:29,610
Dan.

136
00:09:29,693 --> 00:09:30,523
On your feet.

137
00:09:30,606 --> 00:09:31,517
Hey, jackass.

138
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,247
Stop trying to act cool
and get up and fight.

139
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:38,040
This is going down whether
you want it or not. Go ahead.

140
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:39,920
But you can't touch me.

141
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:41,340
I'm Dan of

142
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,777
Steel and none of you can take me down.

143
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:49,817
You don't have what it takes.

144
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:50,730
What the?

145
00:09:50,813 --> 00:09:51,917
What What happened, Mr.

146
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:52,830
Joestar?

147
00:09:52,913 --> 00:09:54,482
He flew back just like that guy.

148
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:57,575
You're an utter fool.

149
00:09:57,760 --> 00:10:00,377
I was about to explain my
powers when you hit me.

150
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:02,657
That impatience nearly
killed your grandfather.

151
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:04,564
I suggest you listen next time.

152
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:08,250
Listen.

153
00:10:08,333 --> 00:10:09,320
My job's not over.

154
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:12,247
I have other important
business to attend to.

155
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:16,145
You really think I would show my
face here just to kill in Yaba?

156
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:17,330
You...

157
00:10:17,413 --> 00:10:18,440
you damn bastard!

158
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:21,797
You told us that your stand is
the lover's, isn't that right?

159
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,240
So tell us!

160
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,871
What the hell does it do?

161
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:29,477
What's the point in telling you
now the battle's already begun, Mr.

162
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:30,390
Joestar?

163
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:33,140
You're all simpletense.

164
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:38,032
You do know no matter how hard you
look, you won't be able to see my stand.

165
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,380
Hey, Half-Pine.

166
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:42,457
You want some cash?

167
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:46,011
It's all yours if he can hit
me in the leg with that broom.

168
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,430
What?

169
00:10:50,513 --> 00:10:52,080
But why would he?

170
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,240
Now hit me!

171
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:59,260
The hell? Now what?

172
00:11:00,940 --> 00:11:01,940
It hurts!

173
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:03,357
I don't get it!

174
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:04,911
It's like I broke my leg!

175
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:07,337
You mean you still haven't figured it out?

176
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:08,577
That's so disappointing.

177
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:12,560
My stand can't be seen because
it's rooted firmly inside you.

178
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:15,057
The moment Inyaba died, it entered you.

179
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:19,258
It got to your brain through your
ear, and that's how I'll get to you.

180
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:29,440
My stand and I are
connected, just like yours.

181
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:34,280
If my stand gets hurt, so do I,
and the reverse is also true.

182
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:37,297
You're utterly helpless.

183
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:39,220
If you so much as scratch me,

184
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:40,460
in that instant,

185
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:43,117
my stand will react to
my pain by going berserk

186
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:45,957
in your head and inflicting
the same agony on you.

187
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:49,377
Not only that, it will deliver
a pain several times greater.

188
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:51,400
Now, I'll say it once more.

189
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:55,782
Alone or together, you won't be
able to lay a single finger on me.

190
00:11:57,600 --> 00:12:01,776
Plus, the Lovers has taken one of
Lord Dio's flesh buds into your body.

191
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:03,897
It's growing in your brain as we speak.

192
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:06,040
Just like it did to Inyaba.

193
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:08,496
It'll devour you from the inside out.

194
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:18,280
I don't recall asking you to strike
me again, you stupid little brat!

195
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:27,660
Well, to be honest, my stand of lovers
isn't as strong as you might think it'd be.

196
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:31,397
It doesn't have the strength to
move even a single strand of hair,

197
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:33,598
making it the world's weakest stand.

198
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:39,732
However, power isn't necessary if all
you want to do is kill your opponent.

199
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,700
Do you understand, gentlemen?

200
00:12:51,300 --> 00:12:53,300
Say something unfortunate happens.

201
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:57,637
Like I get into an accident, a baseball
hits me, or I just trip and fall.

202
00:12:57,720 --> 00:13:00,800
How do you think that would
affect you, Mr. Joestar?

203
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:06,820
I might get banged up some, but your body
would suffer far greater pain than mine.

204
00:13:08,740 --> 00:13:10,300
What the? How?

205
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:13,537
How am I feeling your knuckles
cracking in my prosthetic hand?

206
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:15,502
You've got ten minutes, old man.

207
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:20,112
Then your brain will be eaten through
and you'll be a corpse like in Yabba.

208
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,840
Jotaro, calm down.

209
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,553
Don't do anything rash.

210
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:26,480
Sorry, but no.

211
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:28,857
I'm gonna kill this damn tool so quickly.

212
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:31,234
You won't have enough time to feel pain

213
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:41,840
Kill me before I feel it,
huh? Sounds interesting.

214
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,340
Do it then.

215
00:13:43,620 --> 00:13:45,149
I want to see what happens

216
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:47,501
What are you waiting for, Jotaro?

217
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,560
Come on, let's see it.

218
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:52,077
Just what were you planning to strike?

219
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:54,740
Tell me my face or maybe my throat

220
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,500
What? You mad?

221
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:00,217
Let's see what'll happen.

222
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:02,124
Don't back down on me now, man.

223
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:05,117
Why don't you try busting
a hole through my chest?

224
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:09,906
Or how about you give up on using your
stand and crack my head open with a rock?

225
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:12,596
This one looks like a prime specimen.

226
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,920
It sure looks big enough for the job.

227
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:21,457
You do not want to
underestimate me, pretty boy.

228
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:24,920
When I say I'm gonna
do something, I do it.

229
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:32,390
Jotaro!

230
00:14:32,473 --> 00:14:33,303
Don't do it!

231
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:35,997
You've already seen how
effective his power is.

232
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:38,668
Are you trying to kill
your own grandfather?

233
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:40,577
Uh, this is Jotaro we're talking about.

234
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:41,490
He might be.

235
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:44,980
You dumb good-for-nothing punk.

236
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:55,310
Yotaro!

237
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:59,340
Don't you toy with me, you bastard.

238
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:02,585
After the geezer kicks
the bucket, you're next.

239
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,000
Look out!

240
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:09,720
It'll be your brain that I send
the lovers in to kill. Stop!

241
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:12,393
What the hell do you think you're doing?

242
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,417
This is just insane.

243
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,720
My grandson is being beaten up to save me.

244
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:24,057
We're completely at this guy's mercy.

245
00:15:24,140 --> 00:15:26,669
I can't do anything
while it's in my brain.

246
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:30,879
I remember when that poison ring
was placed around my aorta long ago.

247
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:32,420
But think, Joseph.

248
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:35,034
There's got to be something you can do.

249
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:44,790
Hey!

250
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:47,170
Chotaro!

251
00:15:47,253 --> 00:15:48,317
Keep him away from Mr.

252
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:49,635
Joestar at all costs!

253
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:53,113
We're gonna try and get as
far away from him as possible!

254
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:55,940
I see.

255
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,376
So that's your plan?

256
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:59,637
Putting some distance
between me and the old man

257
